Finding: {"title":"DELETE /micamp/cards/:id has no ownership check at all — any authenticated user can delete any student's stored card","severity":"CRITICAL","area":"Multi-tenant isolation / IDOR","files":["src/server/routes/routes-micamp.ts"],"detail":"L397-435: the route loads the card purely `where: eq(schema.studentPaymentMethods.id, cardId)` — it never checks that `card.studentId` matches the authenticated user, nor that the caller is an admin of `card.flightSchoolId`. Any authenticated user who can guess/enumerate a UUID (or gets one from another leaking endpoint) can delete any other student's stored payment method, and it also fires a live `deleteToken` call against MiCamp for that card.","impact":"Cross-tenant/cross-student destructive action requiring zero authorization beyond having any valid session. Could be used to grief students (delete their card right before a scheduled charge) or as a building block for further abuse.","recommendation":"Require `card.studentId === authUser.id` OR `authUser` is an admin/super_admin of `card.flightSchoolId` before allowing deletion.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

